Make train_mp.py (model parallel) run on Intel XPU under mpiexec.

- train_mp.py: device helpers from utils/device.py instead of torch.cuda.*
  (set_device, synchronize, autocast/GradScaler device, nvtx/profiler shims);
  pynvml replaced by device.memory_used_gb(); transformer-engine imported only
  when that backend is selected; ezpz.setup_torch() when WORLD_SIZE is unset
  (mpiexec on Aurora); tp/cp/order read from the YAML, CLI flags override.
- utils/comm.py: process-group backend from device.dist_backend() (xccl on
  XPU) instead of hard-coded nccl; skip init if already initialized.
- train_mp.py --grad_sync: on non-cuda devices (default 'auto') gradients are
  synced once after backward instead of by DDP during it, so dp collectives
  never overlap the tp/cp ones in backward (that overlap hangs oneCCL).
- ReduceOp.AVG replaced by SUM + divide (train_mp.py, distributed/mappings.py)
  since not every backend supports AVG.

Applies to sc25-dl-tutorial commit 7e91316 (saforem2 sunspot-xpu-support):
  (setup.sh applies it after checking out that commit)

